sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor IA as Account IAM admin
    actor Adm as Deployment admin<br/>(deployer creds)
    actor Op as Benchmark author<br/>(operator creds)
    participant CLI as baas CLI
    participant CFG as ~/.baas/config.yaml
    participant AWS as AWS account

    Note over IA,AWS: The whole life of one deployment, from an empty account to an empty account.<br/>Commands in brackets are not baas commands — the CLI cannot do them.

    rect rgb(240, 240, 255)
        Note over IA,AWS: 0. One-time IAM
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin deployment setup [--region]
        CLI->>AWS: sts:GetCallerIdentity, SimulatePrincipalPolicy
        CLI-->>Adm: rights missing -- the rendered policy JSON on stdout, exit 1, nothing created
        Adm->>IA: hand over the JSON
        IA->>AWS: [attach as customer-managed policy]
        opt CI federation wanted
            IA->>AWS: [deploy cf-template-ci.yaml, or reuse the account's GitHub OIDC provider]
        end
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over IA,AWS: 1. Install
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin deployment setup [--region] [--aws-profile]<br/>[--use-existing-vpc --vpc-id --subnet-id --sg-id]<br/>[--github-org --github-repo --oidc-provider-arn]
        CLI->>AWS: bucket-region check, then the policy step (SimulatePrincipalPolicy)
        CLI->>AWS: CreateStack <prefix>, wait (~1.5 min)
        CLI->>CFG: write prefix, aws.profile, aws.region
        CLI-->>Adm: OperatorRole ARN + "Nobody can assume it yet" + next: build-image
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin image build
        CLI->>AWS: preflight version, UpdateStack (image params), StartImagePipelineExecution
        CLI->>AWS: wait (~15 min), tag AMI, PutParameter /<prefix>/runner/ami-id, retire previous AMI
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin image show
        CLI-->>Adm: version, AMI, parent, built-at, pointer
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 235)
        Note over IA,AWS: 2. Onboard an operator machine
        Op->>AWS: [grant sts:AssumeRole on <prefix>-role-operator -- add role_arn profile to ~/.aws/config]
        Op->>CLI: baas config sync --deployment baas-<accountId>
        CLI->>AWS: DescribeStacks (proves it exists)
        CLI->>CFG: write prefix
        Op->>CLI: baas config set --operator-profile p [--region] [--instance-type] [--timeout]<br/>[--watchdog-margin] [--git-resolve-project]
        CLI->>CFG: write
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over IA,AWS: 3. Measure (repeatable, see baas-run.mmd)
        Op->>CLI: baas run --benchmark-jar b.jar --project p [--tag k=v]… jmh -- Bench -f 1
        CLI->>AWS: upload, reserve the job item, RunInstances, poll the job item
        CLI-->>Op: job id + result table
        Op->>CLI: baas results query [--project p | --all-projects | --job-id id]
        Op->>CLI: baas jobs download <jobId>
        Op->>CLI: baas jobs diff <jobIdA> <jobIdB>
    end

    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
        Note over IA,AWS: 4. Retire
        Adm->>CLI: baas admin deployment teardown [--yes]
        CLI-->>Adm: warns: the bucket, the results table and the image go, none recoverable
        CLI->>AWS: refuse if a runner is pending/running -- empty the bucket -- DeleteStack, wait<br/>(bucket and table go with it) -- then retire the image (pointer, AMI, snapshot, Image Builder records)
        Note over Adm,AWS: Nothing is left behind. Data leaves before a teardown through a future baas admin export.
        Note over CFG: config.yaml still names the prefix, but every command against it now fails:<br/>the stack, the bucket and the table are gone
    end
